NAME
     du - how much disk a tree uses

SYNOPSIS
     du [-s] [-a] [-h] [PATH...]

DESCRIPTION
     du adds up the blocks of everything under each PATH and prints a
     line per directory. The numbers are blocks the files actually
     occupy, so a sparse file counts what it costs and not what it says.

OPTIONS
     -s   one total per PATH and nothing else
     -a   a line for every file, not only directories
     -h   kilobytes and megabytes rather than blocks

SEE ALSO
     df(1), ls(1), find(1)
